{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/pulls/20628","id":3059707280,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAB0Los62X22Q","html_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/20628","diff_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/20628.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/20628.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/20628","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/pulls/20628/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/pulls/20628/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/issues/20628/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/statuses/824a4ab2ba7d3b91b4105c6d701d769757024ef7","number":20628,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"VAR|TMP overhaul","user":{"login":"iluuu1994","id":1752683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTI2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1752683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iluuu1994","html_url":"https://github.com/iluuu1994","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iluuu1994/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iluuu1994/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iluuu1994/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iluuu1994/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iluuu1994/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iluuu1994/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iluuu1994/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iluuu1994/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iluuu1994/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The aim of this PR is twofold:\r\n\r\n- Reduce the number of highly similar TMP|VAR handlers\r\n- Avoid ZVAL_DEREF in most of these cases\r\n\r\nThis is achieved by guaranteeing that all zend_compile_expr() calls, as well as all other compile calls with BP_VAR_R, will result in a TMP variable. This implies that the result will not contain an IS_INDIRECT or IS_REFERENCE value, which was mostly already the case, with two exceptions:\r\n\r\n- Calls to return-by-reference functions. Because return-by-reference functions are quite rare, this is solved by delegating the DEREF to the RETURN_BY_REF handler, which will examine the stack to check whether the caller expects a VAR or TMP to understand whether the DEREF is needed.\r\n\r\n- By-reference assignments, including both `$a = &$b`, as well as `[&$a] = $b`. When the result of these expressions is used in a BP_VAR_R context, it will be passed to a new ZEND_DEREF opcode beforehand. This is exceptionally rare.\r\n\r\nPreliminary testing shows a 1.1% wall time improvement in Symfony Demo and roughly 0.5% in Wordpress. *Edit*: Sadly I can now only measure a 0.15% improvement for Symfony, but 0.8% for Wordpress. Zend/bench.php improves by ~3% in my tests. There seems to be quite a bit of volatility involved, potentially in relation to binary layout. Regardless, I think this is unlikely to cause true slowdowns for code that doesn't use return-by-ref.\r\n\r\nTODOs:\r\n\r\n- [x] Verify this doesn't break important optimizations\r\n- [x] Use `zend_unwrap_reference()`. I missed this function, I was looking for a macro.\r\n- [x] Check why JIT i-count regresses. *Edit*: Symfony Demo now reduces jitted code by 0.35%, Wordpress by 0.02%.\r\n- [x] Try to replace `DEREF` with `QM_ASSIGN`.\r\n- [x] Add checks to `R`/`IS` compile-paths, asserting no `VAR`s are generated.","labels":[{"id":3045702973,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMDQ1NzAyOTcz","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/labels/Category:%20Engine","name":"Category: Engine","description":"","color":"5319E7","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3611286713,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAB0Los7XP9y5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/labels/Extension:%20mbstring","name":"Extension: mbstring","description":"","color":"0052CC","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3611288125,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAB0Los7XP-I9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/labels/Extension:%20opcache","name":"Extension: opcache","description":"","color":"0052CC","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3611400300,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAB0Los7XQZhs","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/labels/SAPI:%20phpdbg","name":"SAPI: phpdbg","description":"","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3685479977,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAB0Los7bq_Yp","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/labels/Category:%20Optimizer","name":"Category: Optimizer","description":"","color":"5319E7","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":7494444148,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAB0Los8AAAABvrQkdA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/php/php-src/labels/ABI%20break","name":"ABI break","description":"","color":"B60205","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-12-01T15:15:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-03T12:44:35Z","closed_at":"2026-01-31T18:44:56Z","merged_at":"2026-01-31T18:44:56Z","merge_commit_sha":"6173a9a10989fa887240590a34c2b0eec50f003e","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"TimWolla","id":209270,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwOTI3MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209270?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TimWolla","html_url":"https://github.com/TimWolla","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TimWolla/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TimWolla/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TimWolla/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TimWolla/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TimWolla/subscri